CLOSURE_CHECKS_CLASSIFIER_AUDIT: {
  "schema_version": 1,
  "migration_run_id": "e6acf649-b95a-42ad-a464-eae802554253",
  "snapshot_timestamp": "2026-05-21T03:23:48Z",
  "ticket_id": "53ef-d6fd-5ca5-4d62",
  "items": [
    {
      "original_text": "plugins/dso/scripts/merge-to-main-pr.sh stamps \"Session-Id: $CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID\" and \"Generated-By: dso-merge-to-main-pr.sh\" trailers into the PR body at create; the value is shell-quote-sanitized before injection; shell unit test asserts both trailer lines are present and that a synthetic newline-containing session ID is rejected at sanitization with a clear error.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes durable system behavior (trailers stamped into PRs with sanitization) and its validation, not a one-time migration task"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "New plugins/dso/scripts/pr-owned-by-session.sh <pr-number> calls gh pr view --json body, parses the Session-Id: trailer, compares to $CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID, and exits 0 (own), 1 (foreign), 2 (absent), 3 (api_error) with structured stderr identifying the case; shell unit test covers all 4 exits with synthetic fixtures; the helper itself never invokes gh pr <destructive>.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system capability (a script with specific behavior and test coverage) that will remain true after implementation"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "New plugins/dso/scripts/pr-destructive-action.sh <pr-number> <action> [args...] is the single permitted path for destructive PR actions: it internally invokes pr-owned-by-session.sh, then on exit 0 executes gh pr <action> [args...], on exit 1/2/3 emits structured stderr with the case identifier and exits non-zero (fail-closed). Shell unit test covers all 4 internal-check outcomes end-to-end.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system capability and control flow mechanism that persists after implementation, despite the detailed technical phrasing"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "New PreToolUse hook plugins/dso/hooks/check-pr-destructive-action.sh parses the Bash tool command string and blocks any invocation containing gh pr (close|merge|edit|comment) that does not also contain pr-destructive-action.sh; hook integration test asserts the block fires on a direct \"gh pr close N\" invocation and does NOT fire on \"pr-destructive-action.sh N close\".",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system capability (hook blocks destructive PR actions unless safeguard is present) phrased as ongoing behavior, though the lengthy description of implementation details creates minor ambiguity"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "CLAUDE.md \"Never Do These\" rule 25 (negative-directive form): \"Never invoke gh pr (close|merge|edit|comment) directly. Destructive PR actions go through pr-destructive-action.sh (the only permitted path). Direct invocations are blocked by PreToolUse hook check-pr-destructive-action.sh.\" Rule additionally documents the exit-code contract (0/1/2/3) and the rationale (session ownership; see fe66-f05b).",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 5,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system constraint and enforcement mechanism that must remain true after implementation"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "All call sites in shell scripts that previously called gh pr (close|merge|edit|comment) directly \u2014 merge-to-main-pr.sh:437/549/1295 \u2014 are migrated to invoke pr-destructive-action.sh. SKILL.md sites \u2014 debug-everything/SKILL.md:1175, phase-10-merge-verify.md:51, end-session/SKILL.md:242 \u2014 are rewritten as negative-directive instruction blocks naming pr-destructive-action.sh as the only permitted path; the rewrite is in addition to the PreToolUse hook (which is the load-bearing enforcement).",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "transitional",
        "ranking": 5,
        "rationale": "describes completed migration of specific call sites and rewrites of documentation, not an ongoing system property"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "CI test under plugins/dso/tests/ scans every .sh file under plugins/dso/ for gh pr (close|merge|edit|comment) invocations and fails the build when any such invocation appears outside pr-destructive-action.sh itself. SKILL.md files are explicitly excluded from this scan (false-positive surface \u2014 prose containing the script name in instruction text would pass meaninglessly per bot-psych analysis). Behavioral compliance on SKILL.md sites is enforced by the PreToolUse hook at runtime, not by the grep test.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 5,
        "rationale": "describes a durable CI system behavior that validates code patterns and excludes specific files, persisting as an ongoing property of the build process"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "Two-session integration test: simulate session A with CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID=session-A-uuid creating a synthetic PR (trailer stamped); switch to CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID=session-B-uuid and attempt close/merge/comment via pr-destructive-action.sh \u2014 all three refused (exit 1, structured stderr). Positive case (session A acts on its own PR) succeeds. Edge case (PR with stripped trailer) returns exit 2 absent \u2014 included in the same test.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "transitional",
        "ranking": 5,
        "rationale": "describes a specific test implementation and execution task with defined success criteria, not an ongoing system property"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "Pre-existing un-trailered PRs migration: a one-shot script plugins/dso/scripts/backfill-pr-session-trailers.sh lists all currently-open PRs and, for each PR whose author matches the local \"gh api /user --jq .login\", prompts the operator to either (a) stamp this user's CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID as the trailer retroactively or (b) skip. Script logs each decision; idempotent (skips PRs that already have a trailer). The migration is operator-driven, never automatic, never claims ownership for a session not actually the owner.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "transitional",
        "ranking": 5,
        "rationale": "describes a one-time migration script execution with logging of completion decisions, not an ongoing system property"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID stability empirical verification (preplanning verification task before sprint dispatch): probe the env var value across (a) initial session start, (b) after one auto-compact event, (c) after a multi-day idle resume if reproducible. Record observed behavior in the epic ticket. If the variable is NOT stable across compaction (the critical Red Team scenario), this epic's primary mechanism is invalid \u2014 the verification task surfaces this before implementation work begins and the design is revised before sprint.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "transitional",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "a one-time verification task with defined completion criteria (probing across scenarios and recording results) that gates whether design revision is needed before sprint work begins"
      },
      "user_decision": "accept",
      "post_migration_section": "CC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "**SC (Probe-6 remediation, architecture-vs-evidence audit 2026-05-16): In-session runtime + operator-action verification.** Before the 53ef sprint can be marked complete, the two runtime/operator dependencies are verified in-session:",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "transitional",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a verification task that must be completed before sprint closure, representing a one-time checkpoint rather than ongoing system behavior"
      },
      "user_decision": "accept",
      "post_migration_section": "CC"
    }
  ]
}

